  "details": "This just in: channel packing exists.\n\nYou already have the source shader that renders the surface the right way. Use that render result. Don't derive transparency on a whim.\n\nIn various cases _MainTex can contain different implementations of colour storage. Thus alpha can contain something that isn't opacity. Wild, I know.\n\nEven the standard unity's PBR shader gives you an option to pack metalness mask into _MainTex.a. Clearly it isn't opacity, but it is treated as one.\n\nSample images provided with and without the word \"test\" scribbled on the stomach area.",
